rything that they were  trying to impress you with and the way  it feels in the hand is gone the  thinness that they brag about on every  new flagship phone when you put that  piece of rubber on top is now gone but  you want to protect the phone what if  you drop it you got to have some sort of  protection on the phone for that right  well turns out the drop tests where they  actually have a case on the phone are  actually at least a little bit useful  because they've shown that basically no  case with a few exceptions basically no  case actually prevents your phone from  getting damaged when you drop it from  any significant height when you drop  your phone on the screen especially is  going to get damaged unless it's an  otterbox defender so really the  protection a case offers is against  direct impact between your phone and  whatever surface you drop your phone on  so if you drop a metal phone on concrete  you prevent that metal from getting  scratched which is great but so do skins  there's skins that you can apply just  like a screen protector it's just on the  back of your phone uh really are thick  enough at this point to actually protect  your phone the same amount as a thin  rubber case would  against the drop from maybe pocket  height  they also tend to improve the feel on  the hand worst case scenario you have  the htc one m8 this is a tall large  rounded metal phone uh and if you want  to touch the top of the phone and grab  that power button with one hand you  inevitably have to do a little shimmy  with your hand and with those smooth  rounded edges that's just asking to drop  your phone eventually so i added a  carbon fiber textured skin to the back  of my phone problem solved and that's  kept the phone's thinness it hasn't  changed the shape of the phone the only  thing that's really changed is the way  it feels in the hand because you now  have that texture so i guess the only  thing you have to worry about is the  actual visual looks of the phone and  that's not really a problem anymore  because a lot of these skin  manufacturers have tons of different  colors and looks and build materials and  all sorts of things for the most popular  phones out there i also have a skin on  my laptop it's a decal from  decalgirl.com don't judge for the  13-inch retina macbook pro obviously  that's a device you don't really drop  that much but it does protect it when i  pull it in and out of my bag from any  scratching with a zipper or something  and at the end of the day if i want to  sell the laptop or get rid of it i can  just take the skin off and it leaves a  metal underneath perfectly new so bottom  line i really don't use cases on my  laptop or tablet or phone and that's  because i actually care about the design  of it and if you do too it doesn't  really make sense to cover that up with  the piece of rubber or plastic so i i'm  going to encourage the the skin makers  out there the d brands the decal girls  the slick wraps all those guys to keep  making more awesome skins for us to  customize our phones the way they look  and the way they feel in the hand  and if i actually need to protect my  phone i'll put it back in my pocket or  get an otterbox defender i guess without  any further ado i'll go ahead and sign  off let me know what you guys are are  you a case person are you a skin person  or do you carry your phone naked because  i know lots of people like it naked

